            "body": "Thanks for sharing!\r\n\r\nThe best ([suggested](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/94cae4660a8b2d95dbbd56e1fbc6fcfa2716d152/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L25-L26)) approach in this use case is in Insert mode to first press `<C-v>` before target pair character to insert it literally. So something like `<C-v>(` to insert `(` and not `()`.\r\n\r\nAlso a note to avoid confusion for future readers: everything in `opts` except `modes` is not a part of 'mini.pairs' and is monkey-patched in LazyVim.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for sharing!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The best (<a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/94cae4660a8b2d95dbbd56e1fbc6fcfa2716d152/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L25-L26\">suggested</a>) approach in this use case is in Insert mode to first press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-v&gt;</code> before target pair character to insert it literally. So something like <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-v&gt;(</code> to insert <code class=\"notranslate\">(</code> and not <code class=\"notranslate\">()</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also a note to avoid confusion for future readers: everything in <code class=\"notranslate\">opts</code> except <code class=\"notranslate\">modes</code> is not a part of 'mini.pairs' and is monkey-patched in LazyVim.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for sharing!\nThe best (suggested) approach in this use case is in Insert mode to first press <C-v> before target pair character to insert it literally. So something like <C-v>( to insert ( and not ().\nAlso a note to avoid confusion for future readers: everything in opts except modes is not a part of 'mini.pairs' and is monkey-patched in LazyVim.",
